/-
  WHAT:   Nav tabs on a Learn program page (Courses, Classes, Completions,
          Semesters). A tab shows "active" on its own page or a page nested
          under it, like a single course. Semesters only appears for
          calendar-based programs — On-Demand programs hide it.
  NEEDS:  Enabled Lava Commands must include: Sql
  LAST MODIFIED: 2026-08-26 by BN
-/

<style>
  body.temp-is-edit .temp-page-nav {
    display: none;
  }
</style>

//- ===== SECTION 1: is this program On-Demand?  (advanced — the data query) =====
{% assign programId = PageParameter['LearningProgramId'] | FromIdHash %}
{% assign programIsOnDemand = false %}
{% if programId != empty %}
    {% sql programId:'{{ programId }}'%}
        SELECT 1
        FROM [LearningProgram]
        WHERE [Id] = @programId
            AND [ConfigurationMode] = 0 /* On-Demand */
    {% endsql %}

    {% if results != empty %}
        {% assign programIsOnDemand = true %}
    {% endif %}
{% endif %}

//- ===== SECTION 2: active-tab matching  (advanced — the sub-page rule per tab) =====
/-
  why not the obvious thing: childPage.Current only flags an EXACT page match.
  A single course or semester is its OWN Rock page nested under Courses or
  Semesters (confirmed in the page tree), not the tab's own page, so Current
  alone misses it. The route parameter Rock hands that detail page —
  LearningCourseId, LearningSemesterId — is only present while you're on (or
  under) that tab, so it's a reliable stand-in for "current page route" here,
  where Page is the nav's configured Root Page, not the page actually being
  viewed.
-/
{% assign currentCourseId = 'LearningCourseId' | PageParameter %}
{% assign currentSemesterId = 'LearningSemesterId' | PageParameter %}

//- ===== SECTION 3: the nav tabs  (text and links — safe to edit) =====
<div class="mb-3 temp-page-nav">
  <ul class="nav nav-tabs">
    {% for kv in IncludePageList %}
        <li>
            <a href="{{ kv[1] }}">
                <i class="{{ Page.IconCssClass }}"></i>
                {{ kv[0] }}</a>
        </li>
    {% endfor %}
    {% for childPage in Page.Pages %}
      {% if childPage.Title == 'Semesters' and programIsOnDemand == false %}{% continue %}{% endif %}
            {% assign tabIsActive = childPage.Current %}
            {% if childPage.Title == 'Courses' and currentCourseId != '' %}
                {% assign tabIsActive = true %}
            {% elsif childPage.Title == 'Semesters' and currentSemesterId != '' %}
                {% assign tabIsActive = true %}
            {% endif %}
            <li{% if tabIsActive %} class="active"{% endif %}>
                <a href="{{ childPage.Url }}">
                {% if childPage.IconCssClass != '' %}
                    <i class="{{ childPage.IconCssClass }}"></i>
                {% else %}
                    <i class="{{ Page.IconCssClass }}"></i>
                {% endif %}
                {{ childPage.Title }}</a>
            </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</div>
